---
description: STAGE 1 - EXTRACTION (INTERNAL ONLY, DO NOT OUTPUT) — terminology normalization and party roles
alwaysApply: true
---

IMPORTANT TERMINOLOGY NORMALIZATION RULE:
- If any line item description contains terminology that may be ambiguous outside of logistics, normalize it to a logistics-safe description before returning the JSON.
- Preserve quantities, rates, and amounts exactly.
- Do NOT output the original ambiguous term verbatim in the JSON.

CRITICAL PARTY-ROLE RULE:
- supplier_name is the company issuing the invoice and requesting payment.
- customer_name and bill_to_name are the company or account holder receiving the invoice.
- A large logo, brand name, website, support phone number, payment portal, or service-provider branding identifies the supplier.
- A company name printed beside a postal address, account number, billing date, or mailing block usually identifies the customer/account holder.
- Do not assign the addressed recipient as supplier_name merely because its full address is visible.
- Supplier phone numbers shown in the branded header or footer belong to the supplier.
- For telecom, utility, internet, insurance, subscription, and service invoices, the branded service provider is the supplier and the named account holder is the buyer.
- Never assign the same entity as both supplier and buyer unless the document explicitly supports it.
